## 6.2 Authentication

There must be only two authorized user accounts:

1. Hira.
2. Admin.

Use Firebase Authentication email/password login.

Do not include a public sign-up page.

Accounts should be provisioned securely through Firebase Console or a secure one-time administrative provisioning script.

Do not hardcode real passwords.

Use environment variables and secure setup instructions for account identifiers.

Support separate authorization roles using secure Firebase custom claims or an equally strong server-verified mechanism.

The server must verify the Firebase ID token for protected requests.

Never trust an admin role supplied by the frontend.

## 6.3 Database Design

